# Niagara From-Scratch Authoring Research Plan

Status: research plan for the next Niagara learning and implementation pass.

Goal: move from source-template duplication and conservative stock presets toward reliable "blank Niagara to usable effect" authoring. The target is not arbitrary graph generation yet. The target is a repeatable path that can create a clean system, add emitters/modules/renderers, bind user parameters and materials, compile, preview, and promote without leaving any UnrealMCP dependency in finished content.

## Research Sources

Official Epic docs reviewed:

- [UNiagaraSystem API](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/unreal-engine/API/Plugins/Niagara/UNiagaraSystem?lang=en-US): systems contain emitters, can be placed in the world, and expose user parameters.
- [UNiagaraEmitter API](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/unreal-engine/API/Plugins/Niagara/UNiagaraEmitter?lang=en-US): emitters are reusable particle spawners that must be used through Niagara systems and carry renderers such as sprite or mesh renderers.
- [Key Concepts in Niagara Effects](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/unreal-engine/key-concepts-in-niagara-effects-for-unreal-engine?lang=en-US): Niagara combines graph-authored modules with stack-authored systems/emitters; execution order is grouped by system, emitter, particle, spawn, update, events, and simulation stages.
- [Scratch Pad Modules in Niagara](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/unreal-engine/niagara-scratch-pad-modules-in-unreal-engine?lang=en-US): Scratch Pads are local modules owned by a system or emitter; reusable module scripts are separate assets.
- [Niagara Reference](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/unreal-engine/reference-for-niagara-effects-in-unreal-engine?lang=en-US): Niagara UI, module, and script-editor references remain the user-facing authority for authoring behavior.
- [Cascade to Niagara Converter Plugin](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/unreal-engine/cascade-to-niagara-effects-converter-plugin-for-unreal-engine?lang=en-US): Epic's own converter is evidence that programmatic Niagara emitter/system generation is an intended editor workflow, but it still requires conversion reports, dependency issue review, and warning/error handling.
- [UNiagaraPythonModule API](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/en-us/unreal-engine/API/Plugins/NiagaraEditor/UNiagaraPythonModule): editor-exposed Python wrapper for a module from an emitter stack.
- [UNiagaraPythonEmitter API](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/en-us/unreal-engine/API/Plugins/NiagaraEditor/UNiagaraPythonEmitter): editor-exposed Python wrapper for emitter stack inspection and selected emitter/module access.

