## Blank Scratch Pad Parameter Write Proof Update

2026-06-30 follow-up target:

- `Python/scripts/analysis/smoke_niagara_blank_scratch_pad_parameter_write.py`
- Temp target prefix: `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/NS_MCP_BlankScratchPadWrite_<run_id>`
- Seed: `create_basic_sprite_niagara_system` with `/Game/MCPWeather/FX/Snow/Materials/M_MCPWeather_Snow_Particle`
- Scratch Pad creation: `create_or_duplicate_scratch_pad_module` without a source, using `target_supported_usage=ParticleUpdateScript`
- Graph mutation: `add_niagara_scratch_pad_parameter_write` adds a `NiagaraNodeParameterMapSet` and writes `Particles.SpriteSize`
- Stack insertion: `add_scratch_pad_module_to_stack` into `ParticleUpdateScript`

Engine-source finding from `NiagaraNodeWithDynamicPins.cpp` and `NiagaraNodeParameterMapSet.cpp`: `AddParameterPin` is public but not exported in a way this plugin can link against. The bridge therefore avoids that call and creates the parameter pin directly, setting `PersistentGuid`, `PinFriendlyName`, and `PinSubCategory=ParameterPin`, while registering `UNiagaraScriptVariable` metadata through the exported `GetAllMetaData()` map path.

Live proof `20260630_blank_scratch_pad_parameter_write_v1` passed:

- Created script: `MCP_BlankUpdateScratch_0`
- Graph mutation: `NiagaraNodeParameterMapSet_0` writes `Particles.SpriteSize` as Vector 2D default `X=36.000000 Y=36.000000`
- Inserted into `ParticleUpdateScript` through `add_scratch_pad_module_to_stack`
- Compile errors/warnings: `0/0`
- Renderer material readback: `/Game/MCPWeather/FX/Snow/Materials/M_MCPWeather_Snow_Particle`
- Promotion audit: ready, forbidden dependency hit count `0`
- Report: `MCPGameProject/Saved/MCP/NiagaraReviews/20260630_blank_scratch_pad_parameter_write_v1/blank_scratch_pad_parameter_write_report.json`
- Generated temp asset was removed offline after editor close; post-clean dry-run selected `0`.

## Blank Scratch Pad User Parameter Proof Update

2026-06-30 follow-up target:

- `Python/scripts/analysis/smoke_niagara_blank_scratch_pad_user_parameter.py`
- Temp target prefix: `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/NS_MCP_BlankScratchPadUser_<run_id>`
- Seed: `create_basic_sprite_niagara_system` with `/Game/MCPWeather/FX/Snow/Materials/M_MCPWeather_Snow_Particle`
- Scratch Pad creation: `create_or_duplicate_scratch_pad_module` without a source, using `target_supported_usage=ParticleUpdateScript`
- Graph mutation: `add_niagara_scratch_pad_parameter_write` adds a `NiagaraNodeParameterMapSet` and writes `Particles.SpriteSize`
- User exposure: `link_niagara_scratch_pad_pin_to_user_parameter` creates `User.MCP_BlankScratchPad_SpriteSize`, sets a Vector 2D default, and links it through a `NiagaraNodeParameterMapGet`
- Stack insertion: `add_scratch_pad_module_to_stack` into `ParticleUpdateScript`

This proof intentionally reuses existing bridge primitives instead of adding another C++ command. The value here is validating composability: fresh blank module creation, internal ParameterMapSet writing, User parameter creation/defaulting, ParameterMapGet linking, stack insertion, compile, renderer material readback, and promotion audit can run as one temp-only authoring chain. The follow-up recipe wraps that same chain in `create_niagara_scratch_pad_vec2_user_parameter_module` so future callers do not need to manually sequence every primitive.

Live proof `20260630_blank_scratch_pad_user_parameter_v2` passed:

- Created script: `MCP_BlankUpdateScratch_0`
- Graph mutation: `NiagaraNodeParameterMapSet_0` writes `Particles.SpriteSize`
- User exposure: `User.MCP_BlankScratchPad_SpriteSize`, Vector 2D default `[42, 42]`
- Graph readback: `NiagaraNodeParameterMapGet_0` outputs `User.MCP_BlankScratchPad_SpriteSize` into the `Particles.SpriteSize` input
- Inserted into `ParticleUpdateScript` through `add_scratch_pad_module_to_stack`
- Compile errors/warnings: `0/0`
- Renderer material readback: `/Game/MCPWeather/FX/Snow/Materials/M_MCPWeather_Snow_Particle`
- Promotion audit: ready, forbidden dependency hit count `0`
- Report: `MCPGameProject/Saved/MCP/NiagaraReviews/20260630_blank_scratch_pad_user_parameter_v2/blank_scratch_pad_user_parameter_report.json`
- Generated temp asset was removed offline after editor close.

Verifier sequencing note: run compile status before full Scratch Pad graph readback for this fixture. A debug-only probe that reopened the generated asset, inspected the full graph, and then requested compile status in the same editor session hit a NiagaraEditor array bounds assert in UE 5.6.1. The passing smoke keeps compile verification before graph readback and does not request another compile-status pass after graph serialization.

## Scratch Pad User Parameter Recipe Proof Update

2026-06-30 follow-up target:

- `Python/tools/niagara_tools.py`
- `Python/scripts/analysis/smoke_niagara_blank_scratch_pad_user_parameter.py`
- Recipe command: `create_niagara_scratch_pad_vec2_user_parameter_module`
- Temp target prefix: `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/NS_MCP_BlankScratchPadUser_<run_id>`

The recipe is a Python orchestration layer rather than new C++. It composes the already verified primitives in one authoring transaction:

- `create_or_duplicate_scratch_pad_module`
- `add_niagara_scratch_pad_parameter_write`
- `link_niagara_scratch_pad_pin_to_user_parameter`
- `add_scratch_pad_module_to_stack`
- optional `inspect_niagara_compile_status` wait

The command returns `write_scope="scratch_pad_vec2_user_parameter_module_recipe"` and keeps per-stage results in the response so smoke tests can still validate each lower-level mutation. This keeps the editor-facing primitive layer available for research while providing a practical one-call route for future blank-system recipes.

